  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Virtual Dance**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Jim's Soliloqy**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Old September Blues**: back after 74 archived shows (1693 days) [4]\n- **Slow Slow**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **Black Metal**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **Call Back**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **End of Run Thru**: rare: 8 archived performances [4]\n- **Touch Me Pt.2**: rare: 7 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **MMJ2011-06-16.MK4** (recommended): source not stated; 28 songs; 152 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Short-lived crackling from the PA system is marked in the recording [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer got a pit ticket; Jim James roamed the whole stage, and the Riverside felt small and intimate [3]\n- The show ended with a double encore totaling four songs [3]\n- Reviews published the day after the show were reportedly all enthusiastic [3]\n- Daniel Martin Moore is credited on vocals; Carl Broemel played electric guitar, pedal steel and saxophone, and Bo Koster keyboards and percussion [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **MMJ2011-06-16.MK4**: taped by Soling; transferred by Soling; source: Schoeps MK41 (DINa) > KC5 > CMC6 > Grace Lunatec V3 > Sound Devices 744t [1]. Also: Recorded with DFC gear and a FOB clamped to the second balcony rail, extended three feet [1]",
